Here is the root cause:
The root cause of the bug is that the OP-TEE node was present in the device tree but was disabled, and there was no reserved memory region declared for OP-TEE. This led the kernel to incorrectly interpret the end of DDR as free memory, which it then used for Contiguous Memory Allocator (CMA) purposes. Since OP-TEE was actually using that memory, it resulted in conflicts and errors when the kernel attempted to access the CMA region.

